note: Steps in a row: ", then", "and then", "and"; "it" is what the step before gave.
let scores be a list of 5, 3 and 9, then sort it biggest first, then say it.
let names be a list of "b", "a" and "c", and then sort it, and then say it.
make a new file called "groceries.txt", then write "milk" in file it,
    then add "eggs" to the end of file it, then add "bread" to the end of file it.
say the contents of file "groceries.txt".
first, say "one".
next, say "two".
after that, say "three".
finally, say "four".
then say "five".
an order has a region (text) and an amount (a number).
let orders be a list of (a new order with region "east" and amount 5), (a new order with region "west" and amount 7), (a new order with region "east" and amount 1).
total the amount of orders per region, then sort it biggest first, then say it.
total the amount of orders and call it everything.
say everything.
average the amount of orders, called mean.
say mean.
count the orders whose amount is over 2 and call it n.
say n.
let big be orders, then count it and call it order count.
say order count.
say "done" and then say "really done".
delete the file "groceries.txt".
